          %h1#composition_laws_for_factorizations Composition laws for factorizations
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#relation_to_awfs"} Relation to awfs
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em composition law
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"} functorial factorization
            is a functorial way to compose lifting structures for its algebraic right maps. A functorial factorization whose pointed endofunctor extends to a monad over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cod
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+weak+factorization+system"} algebraic weak factorization system
            if and only if it has a composition law. Moreover, subject to smallness conditions, any functorial factorization with a composition law freely generates an algebraic weak factorization system.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is a category equipped with a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"} functorial factorization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
            to a factorization
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi L
                    %mi E
                    %mi f
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi R
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \xrightarrow{f_L} E f \xrightarrow{f_R} B
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"} functorial factorization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\mathbf{2}}
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cod
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            (regarded as an object of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\mathbf{2}}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_L
            and the identity:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mi L
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mi R
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi id
                        %mtd
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{ &amp; \xrightarrow{f_L} &amp; \\ ^f \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow^{f_R} \\ &amp; \xrightarrow{id}&amp;. }
          %p
            As with any pointed endofunctor, we can consider the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+pointed+endofunctor"} algebras
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
            equipped with a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mi f
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s : E f \to A
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
